cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "HackAlem AI repository study: pseudonymised data and code"
version: v1.0.2
date-released: 2026-09-28
authors:
  - family-names: Bayan
    given-names: Talgar
    affiliation: "School of Computing and Artificial Intelligence (SCAI), Nazarbayev University; University of Manchester"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tbayan/HackalemAI-Repo-Data-Mining"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23020982  # all versions on Zenodo; v1.0.2 is 10.5281/zenodo.23021335
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Pseudonymised dataset, analysis pipeline and paper sources for the study
  "Measuring AI Coding Agent Use from Repository Traces: Evidence from a
  Hackathon Where Codex Was Required", based on the 3,649 organiser-created
  repositories of the HackAlem AI hackathon (Astana, 23 September 2026).
  Credential findings are included only as aggregates. The analysis of the
  jury's decisions is pre-registered at https://osf.io/bm3je.
keywords:
  - AI coding agents
  - mining software repositories
  - hackathons
  - OpenAI Codex
  - credential leakage
